---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Affiliate & Sponsorship Disclosure | Peaks and Puddles" description="How Peaks and Puddles is funded through affiliate partnerships and clearly labelled brand spotlights.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 pb-12 pt-8">
    <article class="prose max-w-none">
      <h1>Affiliate &amp; Sponsorship Disclosure</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: November 2026</em></p>

      <p>
        At <strong>Peaks and Puddles</strong> (<code>peaksandpuddles.co.uk</code>), our priority is giving parents honest, practical advice on technical kids' outdoor gear, forest nursery kit lists, and family adventures.
      </p>

      <h2>How Affiliate Links Work</h2>
      <p>
        To keep our guides free to read without intrusive pop-up ads, some outbound links to retailers on this website are affiliate links. When you click one of these links and make a purchase, the retailer pays us a small referral commission—at <strong>zero extra cost to you</strong> (the price you pay is identical).
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Amazon Associates:</strong> <em>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</em></li>
        <li><strong>Awin &amp; Outdoor Retail Partners:</strong> We also participate in affiliate programmes run via networks such as Awin, partnering with vetted UK and Nordic outdoor retailers and children's clothing brands.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Editorial Independence &amp; Sponsored Placements</h2>
      <p>
        Affiliate commissions never dictate which waterproof ratings, layering systems, or products we recommend. If an affordable wipe-clean pair of dungarees outperforms an expensive technical shell for everyday nursery mud, we say so.
      </p>
      <p>
        We occasionally partner with carefully vetted outdoor brands for sponsored placements or featured spotlights. In accordance with UK Advertising Standards Authority (ASA) guidelines, any paid placement, gifted sample, or sponsored feature is always clearly labelled on the page.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>